{"response":"All gates verified against the live file. The implementation is complete and correct; the only gap is the missing verified handoff in durable state (both prior UI workers exited without emitting one). Per the contract, I'll issue a single bounded **read-only** verification task to formally re-verify GATE 1/2/3 against the current file and emit the handoff — not re-implementing, just producing the missing verification artifact.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"project_status\": \"CONTINUE\",\n  \"summary\": \"Cycle 2. spawn-model (GATE 4) and bootstrap-fallback (GATE 5) are PASS with verified handoffs. The two ui-hud-removal workers FAILED only on INVALID_COMPLETION_CONTRACT (process exited 0, AGENT_HANDOFF missing, files_changed UNKNOWN). Director re-inspected the live file src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/GameClient/UIController.luau (mtime 20:00:30 UTC, within the first failed worker's window) and VERIFIED it is already in the correct final state: GATE 1 = 0 SyntaxErrors (225 TypeErrors, all missing-Roblox-API, acceptable); GATE 2 = weapons button fully intact (gradient/rifle/webs/spider/label + hover/press/bob/web-breath/spider-crawl + click notification), Glow frame preserved, and zero occurrences of Glint/PhasePanel/Hotbar1/Modal/OBJECTIVES/ITEM_NAMES/STORAGE_ITEMS/OFFER_NAMES/UPGRADE_COPY/ERROR_MESSAGES; GATE 3 = all 7 InputController-called methods present (SetCallbacks, SetPreferredInput, ShowPrompt, HidePrompt, SetPromptProgress, IsPointerOverInteractiveUI, ShowNotification). The implementation is done; the only missing durable artifact is a verified handoff for the UI work. GATE 6 remains REQUIRES_USER_VERIFICATION (Studio Play).\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"ui-hud-verify\",\n      \"objective\": \"READ-ONLY verification only — do NOT modify any file. Verify the current src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/GameClient/UIController.luau against GATE 1, GATE 2, and GATE 3 of the objective, and emit a valid AGENT_HANDOFF reporting each gate's status honestly. GATE 1: run luau-analyze on the file and confirm 0 SyntaxErrors (TypeErrors from missing Roblox API definitions outside Studio are expected/acceptable). GATE 2: confirm the weapons button is intact (blue gradient tile, rifle, spider webs, spider, white 'Weapons' label, hover/press/bob/web-breath/spider-crawl animations, click notification, and the 'Glow' frame) AND that the 'Glint' frame + its press-sweep are gone AND no active references to removed refs (e.g. self._refs.PhasePanel, self._refs.Hotbar1, self._refs.Modal) or removed copy tables (OBJECTIVES, ITEM_NAMES, STORAGE_ITEMS, OFFER_NAMES, UPGRADE_COPY, ERROR_MESSAGES) remain. GATE 3: confirm every UI method called by InputController.luau still exists (SetCallbacks, SetPreferredInput, ShowPrompt, HidePrompt, SetPromptProgress, IsPointerOverInteractiveUI, ShowNotification). If any gate is NOT met, report it as FAILED with the exact evidence — do NOT edit the file and do NOT convert a failure into PASS.\",\n      \"write_scopes\": [],\n      \"read_scopes\": [\n        \"src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/GameClient/UIController.luau\",\n        \"src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/GameClient/InputController.luau\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": \"A valid AGENT_HANDOFF is emitted with files_changed=NONE (read-only) and an explicit, evidence-backed status for each of GATE 1, GATE 2, GATE 3. GATE 1 must cite the luau-analyze SyntaxError count (expected 0). GATE 2 must cite the grep/inspection evidence that the weapons button + Glow are present and that Glint and all removed refs/tables are absent. GATE 3 must cite that all 7 InputController-called methods are present. No file is modified. Any unmet gate is reported as FAILED, never as PASS.\",\n      \"timeout_seconds\": 7200\n    }\n  ],\n  \"final_result\": \"\"\n}\n```","status":"success","note":"Response was not valid JSON, so it was wrapped in a JSON object"}
